.TH BCTEST 1
.SH NAME
bctest \- regression test for bc(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bctest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Bctest
loads
.BR /p9/dis/bc.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR runstring(prog) ,
and checks a representative subset of the programs used to develop
.IR bc (1)
against golden output: arithmetic and its scale/precision rules,
comparisons and logical operators, control flow
.RB ( if / while / for ),
functions with
.BR auto ,
recursion, postfix
.BR ++ / \-\- ,
and the
.BR sqrt / length / scale
builtins. Every expected string was checked once against the host's
real
.IR bc ,
including two that were themselves wrong on first draft and caught by
the test failing against a
.I working
implementation: unary minus binding tighter than
.B ^
(so
.B \-2^2
is 4, not \-4), and a compound assignment
.RB ( += ", etc.)"
being silent exactly like a plain
.B =
rather than printing.
.PP
Also checks the one precision boundary
.IR dc (1)
shares with this program: Limbo's
.B big
is a 64-bit integer, not arbitrary precision, so
.B sqrt(2)
at scale 9 still matches the host exactly, and at scale 10 this program
now fails loudly
.RB ( "precision exceeded" )
instead of silently printing a wrapped-around wrong answer.
.PP
Prints one line per failure to standard error, a final
.IR N " passed, " N " failed"
summary to standard output, and exits with a non-nil status if
anything failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/bctest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR bc (1)
.SH BUGS
Runs
.I bc
in-process via its
.B runstring
seam, not as a spawned subprocess reading real files and standard
input/output \(em so it does not exercise
.IR bc 's
own
.BR init ,
argument parsing
.RB ( -e / -f ),
or file I/O at all.
